#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:15
msgid "Discover separate native revision, archive and duplication post types and fields, revision statuses and active Pro/integration state. Supply post_id for source permissions, available templates and taxonomy assignment choices. Revisions are separate from the published source post. Native capabilities and source read access are enforced."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:16
msgid "Find revisions and past revisions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:16
msgid "Browse a bounded native revision queue or WordPress archive. Filter by source post, status, author or title. Every returned revision and source requires native read access. Other users’ restricted revisions are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:17
msgid "Read a revision source post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:17
msgid "Read one supported revision, archive or duplication source and its revision token before creating a new copy. Requires source read access and native copy_post or edit_post. Does not expose passwords, authentication metadata or signed preview links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:18
msgid "Read a revision"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:18
msgid "Read revision content, its native scheduling dates and terms, plus revisions for both the copy and source. Authentication metadata, passwords and signed preview links are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:20
msgid "Create a new revision"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:20
msgid "Create a native unsubmitted revision of one supported readable source using copy_post permission and the source expected_hash. Native metadata/taxonomy cloning, revision limits, builder gates and hooks apply. Omit changes to copy content unchanged. dry_run never creates a copy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:21
msgid "Duplicate a source post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:21
msgid "Create a native draft duplicate of an enabled readable source post. Requires duplicate_post permission, the source expected_hash and native duplication settings. Copies the native configured fields, taxonomy and metadata through RevisionCreation. dry_run creates nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:22
msgid "Update revision content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:22
msgid "Patch only supplied editable revision fields using expected_hash. Native allowed fields, locks, term/author permissions and sanitizers apply. The published source is unchanged. Submitted or scheduled copies require their native edit permission; all edits to scheduled revisions require approval permission. dry_run validates without saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Mcp/Revisions.php:24
msgid "Submit, approve or manage revisions"
